Security notes
- .env.example exists as a template. Never commit real secrets.
- Use scripts\pre-commit.ps1 to block local commits with likely secrets.
  - Install locally: copy scripts\pre-commit.ps1 to .git\hooks\pre-commit (or set core.hooksPath).
  - Make sure PowerShell can run scripts or run with: powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\pre-commit.ps1
- CI runs .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml to detect secrets on push/PR.
- If the scanner flags something, move it to .env (never committed) or your secret manager (Azure Key Vault, GitHub Secrets, etc.).